--TEST--
`Core\Task::all` composes inside `Core\Task::afterResponse`'s callable with no special case — `rule:concurrency/after-response-outlives-the-connection`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// § 6: "`Core\Task::all`/`::map` compose inside it with no special case, since
// it is an ordinary task." A deferred callable that could not start children
// would work everywhere except the one place the receipts are actually sent, so
// the group is asked for *from inside* the callable rather than beside it — and
// the sum is read back, because a group that answered a shape of nulls would
// print plausibly against a case that only counted its fields.
Core\Task::afterResponse(fn (): void => {
    var $sent = Core\Task::all({
        receipts: fn (): int => 2,
        webhooks: fn (): int => 3,
    });
    echo "sent ", $sent->receipts + $sent->webhooks, "\n";
});
echo "the response\n";
--EXPECT--
the response
sent 5
